{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 27, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "As he slowly opened his eyes, the bright sunlight streaming through the window was blinding. But it wasn't the sunlight that caught his attention - it was the health bar hovering above his field of vision, and the minimap in the corner of his eye. Confused and disoriented, Jack sat up in bed and looked around. The room was familiar, but it was also...off. The furniture was too perfect, the textures too uniform. And then he saw it: a \"Respawn in 5...4...3...\" counter ticking away on the wall. Jack's mind reeled as he scrambled out of bed and staggered to the window. The world outside was just as fake, with NPCs going about their daily routines in a stilted, robotic manner.\n\n*** \nPanic set in as Jack's memories began to resurface. He remembered playing a game called \"Eternal Realms\" on his console, getting to level 27 and pausing the game for the night. He must have gotten sucked into the game, somehow. The implications were mind-boggling. Jack's character, a burly warrior named Grimbold, was level 27 - and he had a quest to complete. With a sense of trepidation, Jack/Grimbold set out into the world, navigating the familiar yet strange landscape. He encountered other players, their names and stats displayed above their heads. They seemed oblivious to his confusion, chatting and trading items as if everything was normal. Jack's mind was racing - how was he going to escape this digital prison, and what would happen if he died in the game?", "logprobs": [{"token": "As", "logprob": -0.07951892912387848}, {"token": " he", "logprob": -0.0349021777510643}, {"token": " slowly", "logprob": -0.03155532851815224}, {"token": " opened", "logprob": -0.00019762947340495884}, {"token": " his", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " eyes", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.00026127262390218675}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.28867143392562866}, {